# ControlRig Authoring Tool Plan

This plan defines the UnrealMCP plugin's editor-only ControlRig authoring
module. It can design, build, validate, and verify ControlRig assets from a
structured recipe, while authored ControlRig, Animation Blueprint, and project
content must not serialize any UnrealMCP dependency.

Target engine: Unreal Engine 5.6.1.

## Goal

Create a project/editor authoring layer that can take a Cubeless rig design
recipe and produce a real ControlRig Blueprint plus optional sample AnimBP
binding:

```text
recipe -> dry-run -> validate -> write -> compile -> readback -> solve proof
```

The tool should let us design and create ControlRigs, not merely poke existing
RigVM pins through MCP. UnrealMCP remains an optional automation caller, not the
owner of the authored asset model.

## Non-Negotiable Boundaries

- No runtime/gameplay module in the first pass.
- No dependency from authored assets to `/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`,
  `UnrealMCP`, `MCPUnreal`, or `mcp_unreal`.
- No project runtime dependency on the authoring module or UnrealMCP plugin.
- No original asset mutation without an explicit Ieta-reviewed mutation plan.
- First implementation writes only `/Game/_MCP_Temp/` or `/Game/_MCP_Sample/`
  targets.
- Do not broaden existing UnrealMCP sample/temp RigVM writers into original
  asset writers.

## Relationship To Existing MCP Tools

Existing ControlRig and AnimBP MCP commands stay authoritative for their current
surface:

| Existing surface | Keep using existing command | New authoring tool role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Static readback | `inspect_controlrig_rigvm_topology`, `inspect_anim_graph_protected_topology`, `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings` | Reuse as independent verification/adapters, not as the builder core |
| Link/default feasibility | `validate_controlrig_rigvm_links`, `validate_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults` | Mirror the validation rules in recipe dry-run and report both route outcomes when invoked through MCP |
| Sample/temp low-level writes | `add_controlrig_rigvm_links`, `set_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults` | Do not duplicate as standalone MCP commands; batch them inside a recipe transaction only |
| Sample ControlRig seed | `ensure_controlrig_sample_asset` | Keep as smoke/sample helper; new tool owns full recipe-driven asset construction |
| Sample AnimBP ControlRig node | `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample` | Keep for narrow sample chain; new tool may later bind authored rigs into sample AnimBPs by recipe |
| Runtime/direct proof | `controlrig_direct_gate_probe`, `sample_controlrig_pre_post_runtime_pose`, `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose` | Reuse after build for evidence |

The new authority is the recipe transaction. It should not expose a pile of
small MCP mutation commands that overlap the existing authority matrix.

