## Authoring Module

Module source path:

```text
MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor
```

Module:

```text
UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor
```

Module type:

- `Editor`
- registered in `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/UnrealMCP.uplugin`
- no runtime module in V1

Build dependencies, expected V1:

- public: `Core`, `CoreUObject`, `Engine`
- private editor: `UnrealEd`, `AssetTools`, `KismetCompiler`,
  `BlueprintGraph`, `AnimGraph`, `AnimGraphRuntime`, `ControlRig`,
  `ControlRigDeveloper`, `ControlRigEditor`, `RigVM`, `RigVMDeveloper`

For Phase 1 dry-run, keep `Build.cs` narrower than this full candidate set and
add AnimBP-related modules only when the AnimBP binding phase actually needs
them.

Explicitly forbidden dependency:

- main `UnrealMCP` module static dependency on `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`

## MCP Adapter Dependency Rule

The authoring module owns the implementation. The main UnrealMCP bridge module
may trigger it only through an optional adapter boundary.

Default adapter path:

- expose JSON-oriented editor functions on the authoring subsystem, for example
  `ValidateRecipeJson`, `DryRunRecipeJson`, and `BuildRecipeJson`;
- call those functions from MCP through Unreal Python or reflection after
  confirming the module/subsystem is loaded;
- return a structured "plugin unavailable" error when the module is absent.

Forbidden adapter path:

- no `UnrealMCP.Build.cs` dependency on `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`;
- no `#include` of `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor` headers from UnrealMCP C++;
- no static C++ calls from the main UnrealMCP bridge module into the authoring
  module;
- no authored asset references to UnrealMCP or MCP-only classes.

If a C++ MCP route is later required, it must be a reflection-only bridge:
load the editor module by name, locate `UClass`/`UFunction` by path/name, pass
JSON strings, and fail cleanly when the module/subsystem is unavailable. The route must not
link against the authoring module.

## Public API Shape

Use a subsystem plus a small static library so UI, Python, commandlets, and MCP
adapters can call the same implementation.

```text
UUnrealMCPControlRigAuthoringSubsystem
UUnrealMCPControlRigRecipeLibrary
FUnrealMCPControlRigRecipe
FUnrealMCPControlRigBuildOptions
FUnrealMCPControlRigBuildReport
FUnrealMCPControlRigValidationIssue
```

Core calls:

```text
ValidateRecipe(Recipe, Options) -> Report
DryRunRecipe(Recipe, Options) -> Report
BuildRecipe(Recipe, Options) -> Report
CompileAndReadback(Targets, Options) -> Report
AuditAuthoredAssetDependencies(Targets) -> Report
```

Reports must be structured and deterministic enough for MCP wrappers to return
them directly.

## Recipe Schema Draft

The recipe should be serializable as UStruct and JSON.

```json
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "target_control_rig_path": "/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigAuthoring/CR_Test",
  "source_skeletal_mesh": "/Game/Characters/Bot/Mesh/SKM_Bot.SKM_Bot",
  "preview_skeletal_mesh": "/Game/Characters/Bot/Mesh/SKM_Bot.SKM_Bot",
  "hierarchy": {
    "import_preview_bones": true,
    "max_import_bones": 256,
    "nulls": [],
    "controls": [],
    "curves": []
  },
  "rigvm": {
    "units": [],
    "variables": [],
    "template_nodes": [],
    "function_references": [],
    "pin_defaults": [],
    "links": [],
    "exposed_pins": []
  },
  "animbp_binding": {
    "enabled": false,
    "target_anim_bp_path": "",
    "source_anim_bp_path": "",
    "control_rig_node": {}
  },
  "verification": {
    "compile": true,
    "save": false,
    "inspect_topology": true,
    "direct_solve": true,
    "dependency_audit": true
  }
}
```

### Hierarchy Specs

Hierarchy authoring should map cleanly to `URigHierarchyController` and
`URigHierarchy` public APIs:

- bones: `URigHierarchyController::AddBone`
- nulls: `URigHierarchyController::AddNull`
- controls: `URigHierarchyController::AddControl`, `FRigControlSettings`
- curves: `URigHierarchyController::AddCurve`
- parent changes: `URigHierarchyController::SetParent`
- control offset/shape/settings:
  `URigHierarchy::SetControlOffsetTransform`,
  `URigHierarchy::SetControlShapeTransform`,
  `URigHierarchy::SetControlSettings`

V1 should support:

- imported preview skeleton roots with bounded bone count;
- direct nulls;
- direct float, bool, transform, and euler controls;
- control shape name, color, initial/global/local transform;
- direct hierarchy curves;
- named parent references that resolve only to already-imported or earlier
  recipe elements.

Defer:

- connectors;
- mirror operations;
- animation channels;
- multi-parent weights;
- arbitrary skeleton retargeting.

### RigVM Specs

RigVM graph authoring should use `URigVMController` through
`UControlRigBlueprint::GetController()` or `URigVMBlueprint::GetController()`.

Known UE 5.6.1 public API candidates:

- `AddUnitNode`
- `AddUnitNodeFromStructPath`
- `AddUnitNodeWithDefaults`
- `AddTemplateNode`
- `AddVariableNode`
- `AddVariableNodeFromObjectPath`
- `AddFunctionReferenceNode`
- `AddFunctionToLibrary`
- `AddExposedPin`
- `SetNodePosition`
- `SetPinDefaultValue`
- `AddLink`
- `BreakLink`
- `RemoveNode`

V1 should support:

- allowlisted unit node script structs only:
  - `FRigUnit_BeginExecution`
  - `FRigUnit_PreBeginExecution`
  - `FRigUnit_PostBeginExecution`
  - `FRigUnit_PrepareForExecution`
  - `FRigUnit_PostPrepareForExecution`
  - `FRigUnit_InverseExecution`
  - `FRigUnit_SetControlFloat` for sample/temp float-control driver recipes
- node names and graph positions;
- pin defaults with the same conservative default policy as
  `set_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults`:
  no array resizing unless explicitly enabled, no linked-pin propagation unless
  explicitly enabled;
- links with cast-node creation disabled by default;
- transaction-level partial-failure reporting.

Defer:

- arbitrary script structs;
- `FRigUnit_InteractionExecution` until an explicit use case is reviewed;
- deprecated `FRigUnit_SequenceExecution`;
- cast-node creation;
- graph replacement;
- comments/reroutes/dispatch nodes;
- function library authoring;
- exposed pins on original assets;
- deleting existing user graph content.

### AnimBP Binding Specs

AnimBP binding should use ControlRig/AnimGraph editor APIs without serializing
UnrealMCP references:

- `UAnimGraphNode_ControlRig`
- `FAnimNode_ControlRig::SetControlRigClass`
- `UAnimGraphNode_CustomProperty::CustomPinProperties`
- `UAnimGraphNode_CustomProperty::SetCustomPinVisibility`
- `FControlRigIOMapping`
- `UAnimGraphNode_Base::ReconstructNode`

V1 should not replace `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample`. Instead, V1
may call the existing sample helper through MCP for smoke testing, while the
plugin implements only recipe validation for AnimBP binding.

Current V1 validation supports:

- `animbp_binding.enabled=true`;
- required read-only `source_anim_bp_path`;
- required sample/temp `target_anim_bp_path`;
- `insert_mode=input_pose_to_controlrig_to_root`;
- bounded `expose_input_pins`;
- bounded scalar/simple-array `input_defaults`;
- orchestration flags matching the existing sample command:
  `disconnect_existing_input_links`, `allow_existing_target_reuse`,
  `overwrite_existing`, and `replace_existing_links`.

`BuildRecipe` deliberately stops before any mutation when binding is enabled.
The safe execution sequence is wrapped by
`build_controlrig_recipe_with_animbp_binding`:

1. validate or dry-run the full recipe;
2. build the ControlRig with `animbp_binding.enabled=false`;
3. call `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample` for the validated sample
   AnimBP target;
4. call `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults` when validated
   `expose_input_pins` or defaults are present;
5. compile the bound AnimBP again after pins/defaults are applied.

V2 should support:

- sample AnimBP ControlRig node insertion;
- explicit input pin exposure;
- input/output mapping;
- default values;
- topology readback and compile proof.

Original AnimBP mutation remains Ieta-review only.

## Build Pipeline

### Phase 0: Analysis And Documentation

Deliverables:

- this plan;
- engine API notes from UE 5.6.1 public headers;
- overlap table against existing MCP commands;
- V1 acceptance criteria.

No C++ or assets in this phase.

### Phase 1: Plugin Skeleton And Dry-Run

Create `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor` as an editor-only module in the existing
`UnrealMCP` plugin with:

- module startup/shutdown only;
- UStruct recipe/report types;
- `ValidateRecipe`;
- `DryRunRecipe`;
- dependency audit helper stub;
- no asset mutation.

Verification:

- UE 5.6.1 editor build;
- no `UnrealMCP` dependency in `.uplugin`, `.Build.cs`, or includes.

### Phase 2: Sample ControlRig Builder V1

Status: partially implemented. Current code creates/reuses sample/temp
ControlRig assets, assigns a preview mesh, adds legacy string-list
curves/nulls/default float controls, adds structured curve/null/control specs
with transforms and parent references, adds allowlisted event unit nodes, adds
the reviewed `FRigUnit_SetControlFloat` sample/temp driver unit, writes pin
defaults and links, compiles on request, and audits for MCP-only references.
It can save temp/sample assets only when `allow_save=true` is supplied through
the options JSON API.

Remaining sample/temp-only write support:

- none for the approved Phase 2 scope.

Verification:

- build a disposable `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigAuthoring/CR_V1`;
- inspect topology;
- direct transient solve proof when units/controls are solvable;
- dependency audit reports no UnrealMCP references.

### Phase 3: MCP Adapter

Add thin MCP access only after the editor tool exists. The first adapter should
be Python/reflection-based so UnrealMCP does not link against the authoring
plugin:

- `validate_controlrig_recipe`
- `dry_run_controlrig_recipe`
- `build_controlrig_recipe`
- `build_controlrig_recipe_with_animbp_binding`
- `validate_controlrig_solver_intents`

The recipe validation/build commands must call the plugin JSON/reflection API
and must not become a second authoring implementation.
`validate_controlrig_solver_intents` is the
exception: it is an UnrealMCP-native validation-only route because it validates
JSON intent metadata only. It must not call the ControlRig authoring module,
load/save assets, or become a RigVM writer.

If a native C++ route is added later for a plugin-backed authoring command, it
must:

- avoid `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor` in `UnrealMCP.Build.cs`;
- avoid authoring module headers;
- locate the plugin and functions dynamically;
- return `plugin_unavailable=true` when the authoring module is absent;
- preserve the same JSON report contract.

Parity gate must ensure every new C++ route has a Python wrapper and docs.

### Phase 4: Presets

Add recipe generators rather than hardcoded builders:

- simple FK control chain; implemented as `simple_fk_control_chain`;
- curve-driven gate controls; implemented as `curve_gate_controls`;
- hand/foot target control; implemented as `hand_foot_target_controls`;
- look-at/aim target; implemented as `look_at_aim_target_controls`;
- two-bone IK limb; implemented as `two_bone_ik_limb_controls`;
- spine/spline control chain; implemented as `spine_spline_control_chain`
  with independent point spaces by default and optional parent chaining;
- interaction target controls; implemented as `interaction_target_controls`;

Each preset produces a normal recipe and goes through the same validation/write
pipeline.

### Phase 5: AnimBP Binding

Add recipe-driven sample AnimBP binding after ControlRig asset authoring is
stable:

- create/reuse sample AnimBP target through existing sample command;
- insert ControlRig node through `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample`;
- expose validated input pins with or without defaults through
  `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults`;
- apply scalar/simple-array defaults through the same command when requested;
- compile/readback through the sample command and post-change compile;
- optional PoseWatch proof.

## Report Contract

Every operation should report:

- `success`
- `plugin_unavailable`
- `dry_run`
- `sample_only`
- `target_control_rig_path`
- `created`
- `reused`
- `target_modified`
- `partial_target_modified`
- `compile_requested`
- `compile_succeeded`
- `save_requested`
- `save_succeeded`
- `dependency_audit_passed`
- `issues`
- `warnings`
- `planned_writes`
- `performed_writes`
- `skipped_writes`
- `reused_items`
- `cleanup_suggestions`
- `created_hierarchy_elements`
- `created_rigvm_nodes`
- `applied_pin_defaults`
- `applied_links`
- `readback_summary`
- `next_action`

On partial failure, `success=false` and `partial_target_modified=true` must stop
any caller from chaining another writer without readback. Validation failures
and JSON/options parse failures must report `target_modified=false`,
`partial_target_modified=false`, `asset_mutation_not_started`, and a
no-mutation `next_action`.

## Verification Gates

Docs-only phase:

```powershell
git diff --check
```

Plugin skeleton or C++ phase:

```powershell
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat' MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development -Project="$Project" -WaitMutex
```

MCP adapter phase:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\controlrig_animbp_mcp_release_gate.py
```

Asset smoke phase:

- create only under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigAuthoring`;
- inspect RigVM topology after write;
- compile and optionally save only temp/sample assets;
- when a UE 5.6.1 UnrealMCP bridge is already running, run
  `uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_controlrig_animbp_binding_bridge.py`
  to verify the sample/temp AnimBP binding composite;
- direct solve proof when requested;
- delete temp assets after the smoke unless the user asks to keep them.

Dependency gate:

- run an AssetRegistry dependency query for every authored package and fail if
  any hard or soft package dependency resolves to UnrealMCP or MCP-only paths;
- load authored packages in the editor and inspect object references, generated
  classes, component classes, graph node member references, and soft object
  paths;
- scan exported text or dependency summaries for `/Script/UnrealMCP`,
  `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCP`, `MCPUnreal`, and `mcp_unreal` as a final
  backstop, not as the only check;
- fail promotion when any hard, soft, generated-class, component, graph-node, or
  package dependency points at MCP-only code.

## Open Questions Before C++ Implementation

1. Should the first plugin live in this MCP test project only, or be mirrored
   later into a `CubelessStylized` checkout as a project editor plugin?
2. Should V1 write only temp assets, or also allow `_MCP_Sample` assets?
3. Which first preset matters most: FK controls, hand/foot IK target, look-at,
   or ControlRig gate controls?
4. Should the first MCP adapter accept raw JSON only, or also named preset
   requests?

## Tivret Instruction

Next implementation pass:

1. Verify with the UE 5.6.1 editor build and source scans proving no
   `UnrealMCP` module dependency and no UnrealMCP -> UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor
   dependency.
2. Start a reviewed Phase 4 preset recipe or Phase 5 AnimBP binding pass.
